// Magic rules, as authored. The "magic.rules" list below is the
// COMPILED form of exactly these -- one input/output pair per key.
//
// chiral keys
//   e   after same-hand key e · after other-hand key
//   r   after same-hand key r · after other-hand key
//   *   after same-hand key   · after other-hand key e
//   @   after same-hand key   · after other-hand key r
//
// adaptive swaps
//   after e, the next @ and * trade places
//   after r, the next @ and * trade places
//   after @, the next e and r trade places
//   after *, the next e and r trade places
//
// alt fingers
//   e* e_* (LT RT) · *e *_e (RT LT) · @r @_r (LT RT) · r@ r_@ (RT LT)
//   *␣ (. RT)
//
